# Starforge design language

A reusable visual and UX system for brand-led product sites. Carry these principles into other web projects to reproduce the same look and feel. Token names may be prefixed per project (this repo uses `--sf-*`); the roles matter more than the prefix.

## Intent

- **Tone:** Apple-style scroll storytelling — sparse sections, one job per section, large expressive type, quiet confidence.
- **Hybrid atmosphere:** Cinematic **deep-space** surfaces for hero/brand moments + quieter **light paper stage** surfaces for reading and explanation.
- **Brand first:** On branded pages, the brand or product name is a hero-level signal, not only nav text. The first viewport should still read as the brand after removing the nav.
- **No dashboard default:** Prefer one composition per viewport over card grids, stat strips, and admin chrome.

## Composition

### First viewport (hero)

Usually contain only:

1. Brand (display weight)
2. One headline
3. One short supporting sentence
4. One CTA group (primary + optional ghost)
5. One dominant visual focal object

Do **not** put product grids, stats, schedules, promo chips, badges, or secondary marketing blocks in the first viewport.

### Section rhythm

- **One job per section:** one purpose, one headline, usually one short supporting sentence.
- Alternate or sequence **space hero** → **paper stage** → **space list/detail** as needed; keep contrast intentional.
- Prefer full-bleed atmospheric planes over inset media cards.
- Default: **no cards**. Cards only when they are the container for a clear interaction. If removing border/shadow/radius does not hurt understanding, do not use a card.
- Detail views always offer a clear path back to the primary landing (“Back to …”).

### Navigation shell

- Keep an app shell (ambient background + sticky nav) mounted across in-app routes — no full document reload for primary navigation.
- Prefer soft, full-width hover mega panes over dense dropdowns.
- Menu content should be **data-driven**, not hard-coded product rows in templates.

## Typography

| Role | Font | Use |
|------|------|-----|
| Display | **Sora** | Brand, nav wordmark, headings |
| Body | **Manrope** | Body copy, UI labels, leads |

- Do **not** switch to Inter, Roboto, Arial, or system stacks.
- Display headings: heavy weight (700–800), tight tracking (`letter-spacing: ~-0.03em` to `-0.04em`), short measure (`max-width` in `ch`).
- Body: ~1.06–1.125rem, line-height ~1.55–1.7, muted secondary color for supporting copy.
- **Eyebrows:** small caps-style labels — uppercase, wide tracking (`~0.14em`), semibold; use accent on dark surfaces and a darker stage-eyebrow token on light paper.

## Color and atmosphere

Cool **starlight / teal-metal** accents. Never default to purple-on-white, purple glow, or generic AI gradient themes.

### Token roles (implement as CSS variables)

| Token role | Purpose | Example dark | Example light / stage |
|------------|---------|--------------|------------------------|
| `bg` | Page void | `#07090f` | `#f3f0ea` |
| `bg-elevated` | Raised surface | `#0e121c` | `#ffffff` |
| `bg-stage` | Paper stage | `#f4f2ec` | `#ffffff` |
| `text` / `text-muted` | Primary / secondary on void | `#e8ecf4` / ~68% alpha | `#12141a` / ~70% alpha |
| `stage-text` / `stage-muted` | Copy on paper | `#12141a` / muted | same family |
| `stage-eyebrow` | Labels on paper (must contrast) | `#1a4a58` | `#1f5565` |
| `accent` / `accent-strong` | Teal starlight | `#7eb6c9` / `#a8d4e0` | `#2f6f82` / `#1f5565` |
| `metal` | Secondary meta | `#9aa4b2` | `#5c6675` |
| `border` / `border-strong` | Hairlines | low-alpha text | low-alpha ink |
| `hero-gradient` | Deep-space plane | blue-black diagonal | same family, slightly lifted |
| `stage-gradient` | Paper plane | warm off-white vertical | white → cream |

### Themes

- Support **dark and light** (`data-theme` on `html`, persisted). Both must remain viable.
- Hero/media planes may stay deep-space even when the site chrome is light.
- Focus rings: accent outline, visible offset.

## Surfaces and controls

- **Hero CTAs:** Pill radius (`border-radius: 999px`). Primary = light fill / dark ink on space; ghost = translucent border, no fill.
- **List rows / interactive rows:** Soft radius (~1.1rem), thin border, elevated mix background; hover lifts slightly (`translateY`) and strengthens border — not heavy multi-layer shadows.
- **Borders:** Prefer 1px low-alpha lines over thick frames.
- Avoid rounded-full pill clusters, emoji decoration, and stacked drop shadows.

## Motion

- Prefer `opacity` and `transform` only.
- Signature ease: `cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1)`; duration ~220ms UI / ~480ms larger transitions.
- Use ambient motion (parallax, slow orbits, scroll reveals) for presence — not noise.
- Honor `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`: disable loops, glitches, and non-essential animation; keep layout readable.
- Route changes may use view transitions with the same ease/duration tokens.

## Hero focal object (space emblem)

The hero may include one **deep-space focal object** beside the copy (orbits + core). Pattern used here:

- Soft elliptical **orbit rings** (teal hairline strokes, slow opposite-direction spin).
- A **static solid core** (CSS radial planet: highlight at ~30% 30%, white → teal → deep teal, soft edge fade). Does not rotate.
- Optional **wireframe phase** (canvas lat/lon mesh only): cool starlight strokes `rgba(168, 212, 224, …)`; matches core size; no body fill under the mesh.
- Cycle example: long solid dwell → short wireframe; brief TV-style signal-loss glitch at transitions.
- Mutual exclusivity: only one of solid core or wireframe canvas visible at a time.
- No cards, badges, or promo chips overlaid on the focal object.
- Glow belongs in the solid gradient itself — do not add a square-clipped halo that reads as a box.
- When reducing motion: static solid core only.

When porting: keep the *roles* (orbits + static lit core + optional wire mesh + short glitch). Exact timings and canvas files can differ.

## Content voice

- Sparse, precise, inviting — not salesy or oversold.
- Prefer “building / growing / expanding” framing for unfinished work.
- Status language stays quiet (e.g. available / building / retired) and does not dominate the layout.

## Anti-patterns (do not)

- Generic dashboard layouts or purple-gradient “AI product” defaults.
- Warm cream + terracotta serif brochure clichés unless the brand explicitly requires them.
- Broadsheet/newspaper dense columns as the default marketing layout.
- Hero overlays: floating badges, stickers, chips, or callout boxes on media.
- Replacing the hybrid space/paper system with a flat single-color app shell.
- Hard-coding catalog or nav product rows when a data source already owns them.
- Inter / Roboto / Arial / system UI font stacks for brand surfaces.

## Porting checklist

When applying this language to another project:

1. Define CSS variables for the token roles above (any prefix).
2. Load **Sora** + **Manrope** (or document an approved substitute pair that is still expressive and non-default).
3. Implement `data-theme` dark/light with viable contrast on both void and paper stages.
4. Build the first viewport as one composition: brand, headline, lead, CTAs, focal visual.
5. Alternate space and paper sections; one job each.
6. Wire sticky shell + in-app navigation without full reloads where the stack allows.
7. Add motion with the shared ease; gate with `prefers-reduced-motion`.
8. Keep accents in the teal-metal / starlight family unless the new brand explicitly remaps the accent role.

